<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">South African Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1934</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South African Party was a political party founded in 1911 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-botha">Louis Botha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-smuts">Jan Smuts</a>, whose leaders governed the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 1910 to 1924. It sought reconciliation between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaners</a> and English-speaking South Africans within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and absorbed the Unionist Party in 1920. In 1934 it merged with Hertzog's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> to form the United Party.</p></div>
